 *  sheet's terms), and `cap` with two decimals, or null for no cap — each dated one as in force on the
 *  sheet's today; and `dated`, every value recorded for the dated settings by key (clerk-limit, floor,
 *  terms, terms-<grade>, grace-<grade>, late-pct, cap, proof-threshold, proof-threshold-<grade>, note-threshold), oldest from-date first; and `proofThreshold` with
 *  two decimals, or null for none, as in force on the sheet's today; and `perms`, the roles set for each
 *  action of the permission matrix, comma separated (an action not in it keeps the standing rule); and `graceDays`, the grace days, or null when off (not dated); and `delegations`, every delegation of the steward role, oldest first; and `noteThreshold` with two decimals, or null for none, as in force on the sheet's today; and `entryDate` (yyyy-mm-dd), or null when off: while set, the default date of a new claim in place of the sheet's today (not dated); and `gradeGrace`, the grace days set per grade in force on the sheet's today (a grade not in it has none; dated, under grace-<grade>); and `gradeProof`, the proof threshold set per grade with two decimals in force on the sheet's today (a grade not in it uses the sheet's; dated, under proof-threshold-<grade>); and `pot` with two decimals, or null for none: shared out among the members of each balanced pool (not dated); and `parent`, the parent sheet's id, or null for none: a grade with no rate in force on a date on this sheet takes the parent's then, up to three levels up (not dated). */
/** A delegation of the steward role: the user acts as a steward while the sheet's today is from
 *  `from` to `to` (yyyy-mm-dd, inclusive), for the steward `by` who delegated. */
export type DelegationEntry = { name: string; from: string; to: string; by: string };

